<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1756">1756</a>–<a href="/years/1791">1791</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart was a composer born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salzburg">Salzburg</a> who settled in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienna">Vienna</a> in 1781 and became one of the greatest figures of the Viennese Classical style. A child prodigy who toured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>, he wrote over 600 works, including the operas The Marriage of Figaro, Don Giovanni and The Magic Flute, symphonies, piano concertos and chamber music. He died in Vienna at the age of thirty-five, leaving his Requiem unfinished.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/wolfgang-amadeus-mozart.jpg" alt="Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Johann Nepomuk della Croce · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Mozart_Family_-_Wolfgang_Amadeus_Mozart_headshot.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>In the eighteenth century Charles Theodore's court at Mannheim, with its celebrated orchestra and its Academy of Sciences founded in 1763, was a leading centre of music, where the young <b>Mozart</b> sought employment in 1777–1778.</blockquote><a href="/empire/electoral-palatinate">Electoral Palatinate · Global &amp; Regional Impact</a></li><li><blockquote>…architecture of Johann Bernhard Fischer von Erlach and Johann Lukas von Hildebrandt, the Karlskirche, the Belvedere and the abbey of Melk defined a Central European style, and in the later eighteenth century Christoph Willibald Gluck, Joseph Haydn and <b>Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart</b> created the Viennese Classical style in music.</blockquote><a href="/empire/habsburg-monarchy">Habsburg Monarchy · Global &amp; Regional Impact</a></li><li><blockquote>He inspired works from Racine’s Mithridate to <b>Mozart</b>’s opera Mitridate, re di Ponto.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-pontus">Kingdom of Pontus · Global &amp; Regional Impact</a></li><li><blockquote><b>Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart</b> died after a short illness, leaving his Requiem unfinished.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/december-5">5 December in history</a></li><li><blockquote><b>Mozart</b> was born there in 1756 and served Archbishop Hieronymus von Colloredo.</blockquote><a href="/state/prince-archbishopric-of-salzburg">Prince-Archbishopric of Salzburg</a></li></ul></section>
